<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Bevcon raises year shr, offers scrip div.</title>
<headline>Bevcon raises year shr, offers scrip div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     764.13	vs  708.86</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 291.10	vs  253.50</p>
<p>    Equity accounted	571.5	 vs  519.6</p>
<p>Retained earnings</p>
<p>	of associates	 288.9	 vs  242.6</p>
<p>    Div income		283.1	 vs  242.6</p>
<p>Div payable June 3</p>
<p>on register May 30</p>
<p>Full name: Beverage and Consumer Industry Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had decided to award capitalisation shares. Shareholders may elect to receive a cash dividend instead. The number of new ordinary shares will be determined by the ratio that 291.10 cents multiplied by 1.06 bears to the weighted average price of the company's share on the JSE for the four days ending June 26.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
